; fish-base vertex: O = incenter of triangle abd, sitting ON the ac-diagonal.
; The emergent 4th ray is the diagonal's CONTINUATION O -> c — the OPPOSITE
; ray of the given a-ray's own line (a tier-2 completion under derive's
; two-tier rule). Both line-new candidates fold a flap off the paper, so
; after the feasibility filter O -> c is the only completion left and any
; toward point picks it (here .b, right of the spine).

paper square

mark --diag = map .a onto .c
mark --ray = through .a .c

step left
mark --l1 = map --ab onto --diag
mark --l2 = map --da onto --diag
flatten (--l1 & .b) (--l2 & .d) (--ray & .a) {toward .b}

; assert faces = 6
